# Project instructions for Keystone Agents

Copy this file to `KEYSTONE.md` at your repository root — OpenCode picks it
up automatically via the `instructions` field in `cli/opencode.config.json`,
the same way Claude Code reads `CLAUDE.md`.

## What goes here

- Build/test/lint commands specific to this repo
- Architectural conventions the agent should follow (and avoid)
- Anything a new engineer would need explained before their first PR

## Example

```
## Commands
- Install deps: `pip install -e ".[dev]"`
- Run tests: `pytest tests/ -v`
- Lint: `ruff check . && ruff format --check .`

## Conventions
- No bare `except Exception: pass` — log at minimum (see src/sandbox/security.py for the pattern)
- New DB models need a real Alembic migration, not just a model class change
- Sandboxed code execution goes through src/sandbox/manager.py — never shell out directly
```
